//! The `view-transition-name` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! specifies the [view
//! transition](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/View_Transition_API) snapshot that
//! selected elements will participate in. This enables you to animate those elements separately from
//! the rest of the page, which uses the default cross-fade animation during a view transition. You
//! can then define custom animation styles for these elements.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: The selected element will not participate in a separate snapshot, unless it has a parent
//! element with a `view-transition-name` set, in which case it will be snapshotted as part of that
//! element.
//!
//! Grammar: none | <custom-ident>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-view-transitions-2/#propdef-view-transition-name
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/view-transition-name
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

